2026-10-25T02:36:58.2995090Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3033800Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3036870Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3042230Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3054940Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3060960Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3066790Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3067150Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3067600Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3067820Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3067940Z If you would like to
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3068270Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3068450Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3068700Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-25T02:36:58.3070470Z   $ sh ./install-nix
